@[boot-loader step]
Now it is time to set up a boot loader, which starts the kernel when the
machine boots. This ISO provides GRUB (the @[grub2] cache, selected in the
@[spell-caches] step and installed in the @[basesystem] step); it works on
both BIOS and UEFI machines.

For the GRUB instructions, type @[todo grub] (or just @[next]).

To see the instructions for this step again, just type @[todo].

When you are finished, type @[next].
